        🔴 THE UNDERLYING CONSTRAINT IS REAL AND IS THE REASON NO FIX WAS ATTEMPTED HERE:
        acquisition and disposition need OPPOSITE orders on the values they SHARE. Acquisition now
        ends ... Signed -> Sent; disposition ends ... Sent -> Signed. ONE master picklist order
        cannot satisfy both directions for the same shared pair at once, so there is no reordering
        of Status__c that fixes the acquisition side without breaking this one.

        WHAT IS STILL GENUINELY UNVERIFIED, RECORDED HERE RATHER THAN ASSUMED IN EITHER DIRECTION:
        whether the Path's bubble order and the Status__c field's edit-form DROPDOWN order are
        actually driven by this master field's value order at all, versus by each record type's
        own picklistValues order (Acquisition_NDA's was reordered to Pending, Received, Signed,
