        STEP ORDER IS STILL NOT WHAT DRIVES BUBBLE ORDER (see the paragraph above this one) - the
        Status__c picklist's record-type-scoped value order does that. This file's step order is
        kept in step with it for readability, per that same paragraph's standing instruction.

        =====================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-25, LATER THE SAME DAY - THE 'Review' STEP IS REMOVED. THE PATH IS NOW
        Prepare -> Approved -> Sent -> Signed, PLUS Declined. FOUR STEPS AGAIN, NOT FIVE.
        =====================================================================

        The user removed 'Review' from the Disposition_NDA record type in Setup a few hours after
        adding it; the measured value list is in that record type file's second 2026-08-25
        amendment. A Path step whose picklistValueName is not on the record type does not render,
